# Local agent/tooling working directories. Not project source: .raven holds
# session state and pre-compact caches, .artifacts holds QA screenshots. Both
# were untracked AND unignored, so any `git add -A` would have swept several MB
# of local scratch into a commit.
#
# Unanchored on purpose — these also appear per-app (apps/api/.raven,
# apps/dashboard/.raven, apps/affiliate/.raven), which a leading-slash rule
# would miss.
.raven/
.artifacts/

# `node_modules/` above matches DIRECTORIES only, so a node_modules SYMLINK is
# not ignored — pnpm/workspace tooling leaves those around, and `git add -A`
# would happily commit the link. The slash-less form catches both.
node_modules
